{#
  The mark that says a document is the publisher's own text.

  Only the official side is ever marked. A summary, a glossary, an index —
  anything written here — carries nothing, because marking both sides would
  put a badge on every card in the library and a badge that is everywhere
  stops being read. So the presence of this mark is the claim; its absence is
  not a counter-claim, just silence.

  Called from the content cards on a game's overview and from the header of
  the document itself, which are the two places a reader decides whether what
  they are about to read can settle an argument.
#}

{% macro officialMark(isOfficial) %}
  {%- if isOfficial -%}
    <span class="official-mark">Official</span>
  {%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}
